A||||5||rodmcneill||Auto. tranny strong enough?||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||03-22-2001||09:35 AM||||Will the standard 125 auto. transmission hold up to the added hp.- torque of the Cadillac engine swaps being discussed?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cozmo||03-22-2001||10:26 AM||||IF the Tranny is in good mechanical condition to start with you should have no problem.  Since you will have the thing out when you do the swap, put a shift kit in.  They not only firm up the shift engagement and increase shift point RPM, they cause less wear on the internal clutches.<BR>C02M0||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||03-22-2001||03:30 PM||||Just dont try to spin the tires or anything like that, that is alot of power on the Tranny and i doubt it would hold up<P>e-mail  Joe at bublucy@sympatico.ca  he would know<P><BR>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||03-22-2001||04:29 PM||||The trans holds up for Chevy V8 why not cadillac?||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||03-22-2001||07:21 PM||||I'd rebuild the tranny while it's out. Then you know for sure all the clutches and bands are good. For a V8 I'd probably replace the chain as well.<P>You can get the parts from <A HREF="http://www.txchange.com/" TARGET=_blank>Transmission Exchange Co.</A> but this is a bigger job than just throwing parts at it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||KRMFiero||03-22-2001||11:00 PM||||Is there away I could change the gear ratio in mine for more top end?<P>Kyle||||reg||1
